+## Example of how to fast replace many redundant entries (e.g. 400+ strategy entries to obsolete anyways etc) using regexp (with chatgpt 5's help anyways etc) and vs code anyways etc
+
+This is a very nice idea i got since i knew thanks to those who taught me about regexp but anyways etc, but i was doing this task of replacing the old strategy entries now not used in our mod for most if not all as tedious and outdated for most if not all but anyways etc, but there are 400+ entries (found using global search of `<Strategy>` anyways etc)! And it's always the same task, i started to do it manually for the first few dozen entries but it's extremely tiring xd if i may say but anyways etc.
+
+Entries are like this
+
+```xml
+<Strategy>TXT_KEY_BUILDING_JAIL_STRATEGY</Strategy>
+```
+
+to all convert to the same xml field to obsolete them but anyways etc:
+
+```xml
+<Strategy>TXT_KEY_DUMMY_EMPTY_CUSTOM_TXTKEY_STRATEGY</Strategy>
+```
+
+So then i got the nice idea to ask chatgpt 5 since i don't know too much about regexp and tedious to do so, and it provided me this search regexp code if i'm not mistaken anyways etc:
+
+```xml
+(<Strategy>)(?!\s*TXT_KEY_DUMMY_EMPTY_CUSTOM_TXTKEY_STRATEGY\s*)([\s\S]*?)(</Strategy>)
+```
+
+Which works perfectly to selectively search strategy xml fields that are not txt key dummy yet, so now i can blindly find and replace file per file for those i want to, saves me a lot of time and headache, i so love ai xd it will really save humanity at least me xd maybe and thanks a lot chatgpt 5 if i may say but anyways etc, hopefully helpful, anyways etc.
